# Response headers for the deployed site, applied by Workers Assets in front
# of the Worker. Vite copies public/ into dist/client/, which is the assets
# directory wrangler uploads — so this file IS the deploy's header policy.
#
# The CSP is the precondition core-assist-byok.md named: once the user's
# OpenRouter key lives in this origin's localStorage, an injected script is a
# credential theft rather than a defacement. `script-src 'self'` is the
# directive that matters, and the codebase already earns it — the only
# `innerHTML` uses in src/ are clears, everything renders through Lit
# templates (which escape), assistant markdown is parsed to an AST and emitted
# as templates with no HTML sink, and the precompiled Ajv validators exist
# precisely so nothing needs `eval`.
#
# `style-src` keeps 'unsafe-inline' and that is a deliberate, bounded
# exception: index.html carries a six-line inline <style> and Lit templates
# set `style=` attributes throughout. CSS cannot read localStorage, so it is
# not on the path this policy exists to close; dropping it would mean
# nonce-stamping the shell for no gain against this threat.
#
# connect-src names openrouter.ai because that is the point of BYOK: the
# browser talks to the model provider directly, on the user's own key.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://openrouter.ai; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
